cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "RU-PlumeScan: catalogue of methane anomalies over the West Siberian Plain from TROPOMI/Sentinel-5P, 2019-2025"
message: "If you use this catalogue or code, please cite both the accompanying paper and this dataset."
type: dataset
authors:
  - given-names: "Oleg"
    family-names: "Sizov"
    affiliation: "Oil and Gas Research Institute of the Russian Academy of Sciences (IPNG RAS)"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-08-09"
license: CC-BY-4.0
license-url: "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/"
keywords:
  - "TROPOMI"
  - "Sentinel-5P"
  - "methane"
  - "CH4"
  - "plume detection"
  - "gas flaring"
  - "West Siberian Plain"
  - "Google Earth Engine"
  - "atmospheric composition"
  - "remote sensing"
abstract: >-
  A catalogue of 122 methane anomalies detected over the West Siberian Plain in
  TROPOMI/Sentinel-5P L3 XCH4 data for 2019-2025. Detection uses a per-overpass
  local annulus z-score built on robust statistics (median and median absolute
  deviation) on an equal-area 5.5 km grid, rather than compositing or an
  absolute concentration threshold. The area of interest is defined
  physico-geographically, by the boundary of the West Siberian Plain. Each event
  carries signal strength, geometry, ERA5 wind conditions, nearest candidate
  source, artefact classification, full processing provenance, and binary match
  flags against two independent catalogues. The package includes the catalogue
  in CSV and GeoJSON, a dictionary of all 59 fields, the methodology
  description, the source code, and the paper figures. Note that the
  independent catalogues used for cross-checking are not ground truth: they
  target gas-field super-emitters and systematically omit flaring, which the
  package documents explicitly.
